{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_b24b23ff187da7326df112088f851726de351373db6fce4bdcbec5194197115a"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Documentation describes cost-aware routing across LLM providers with automatic failover, a smart routing proxy (fuxi proxy), and fork agents with a default fork concurrency of 4 (FUXI_FORK_MAX_CONCURRENCY)."},{"claim_ids":["clm_de0125b1027710e4759bf0c58e9c6d1703e655f983fcad6e46a975fef87d011b"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Configuration resolves with precedence environment variables > ~/.fuxi/config.yaml > built-in defaults, and config changes are said to hot-reload while the agent runs."}],"claim_ids":["clm_b24b23ff187da7326df112088f851726de351373db6fce4bdcbec5194197115a","clm_de0125b1027710e4759bf0c58e9c6d1703e655f983fcad6e46a975fef87d011b"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T02:01:12Z","created_by_operation":"op_f58d8eef1ae04d8b9b8bb91c9ed483f1","id":"pg_b1d3df712bcf5cafbae7b1b036caa66c","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/fuxicodex-fuxi-docs-environment-md-ab2785904754-b1b036caa66c.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_4193a7cb2ab75a0185c0209baf69e809"],"title":"fuxicodex/Fuxi/docs/environment.md @ ab2785904754","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:01:12Z","updated_by_operation":"op_f58d8eef1ae04d8b9b8bb91c9ed483f1"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_1ed1e451ac0798b98b6ec6988e60c30f7fe95b1295ba005cb4d95d63a9a993da"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"FuXi is documented as a terminal AI coding agent built in Go, shipped as a single static binary with no runtime dependencies, positioned as a provider-agnostic alternative to Claude Code."},{"claim_ids":["clm_5bb1f3847f4984638c76a18d3c27a8df1cddf1c5ee443a5c338165a44b9d0a38"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The README reports a self-run head-to-head benchmark against another coding agent using an objective pytest+coverage scorer across 15 micro and 4 large-project dimensions, and explicitly cautions it is a small, non-third-party task set measuring the agent loop."},{"claim_ids":["clm_639ee5fabe7c55abd2aa268bd6483507d749312f36ab51860a108e802933efe4"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The agent is described as running a Think → Act → Verify loop: it reasons about a task, acts with built-in tools, inspects results, and iterates until the work is verified."},{"claim_ids":["clm_6920e1412e414365b7e7e3f04f6a409ff062ee2b2d8713a9ea02e329e5c722c7"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Sessions are described as durable: transcripts persist to disk, checkpoints allow resume, rollback, or fork, long conversations auto-compact, and an idle 'dreaming' pass consolidates memory across sessions."},{"claim_ids":["clm_69f246579dd0af64583445181b87e87579175c693e7815b8d8477d26624cf843"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Shell commands reportedly pass an AST safety classifier and rule set before execution, with fine-grained permissions and audit logging; permission modes are default, plan, and bypassPermissions, plus a classifier-gated --auto mode with a circuit breaker."},{"claim_ids":["clm_6e0c0c38c0c4e4d787c181c835eee9e04bc4f7681f58cab2beb5430df9300ac9"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The product exposes a TUI with slash commands (/model, /config, /cost, /usage, /context, /compact, /permissions, /commit, /review, etc.) plus CLI subcommands such as fuxi doctor, verify, wizard, update, proxy, and mcp serve."},{"claim_ids":["clm_a300fbc4166ce220b18aafa906be1ee3ecccd6905726b07d1adadc51aaa8f197"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The repository hosts only documentation, release installers, and the issue tracker; the product source is proprietary and not published here, under a proprietary license."},{"claim_ids":["clm_ab8341aabfd3ebff291e36f706f043ee5f89a1b5f9cf9286ef4457378de024b1"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The project states it currently ships without published scores on third-party benchmarks such as SWE-bench or Terminal-Bench, and instead offers a do-it-yourself evaluation checklist plus in-TUI /cost, /usage, /context, and /status commands."},{"claim_ids":["clm_b24b23ff187da7326df112088f851726de351373db6fce4bdcbec5194197115a"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Documentation describes cost-aware routing across LLM providers with automatic failover, a smart routing proxy (fuxi proxy), and fork agents with a default fork concurrency of 4 (FUXI_FORK_MAX_CONCURRENCY)."},{"claim_ids":["clm_bd5f199b443d927b519e8170830ebb4e569be917b8e713abee7f7923d0a21f1e"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Documentation claims 50+ built-in tools including file read/write/edit, bash and PowerShell shell, ripgrep search, web fetch, LSP diagnostics, Jupyter, browser use, background tasks, and parallel sub-agents."},{"claim_ids":["clm_d0e8c9ab428966612f3c83877527df401f3cedcfe59eb36b03befe04d55e2c91"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The agent is documented as provider-agnostic: it accepts any OpenAI-compatible endpoint, Gemini, Bedrock/Vertex keys, or FuXi OAuth login, and acts as an MCP client."},{"claim_ids":["clm_de0125b1027710e4759bf0c58e9c6d1703e655f983fcad6e46a975fef87d011b"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Configuration resolves with precedence environment variables > ~/.fuxi/config.yaml > built-in defaults, and config changes are said to hot-reload while the agent runs."}],"claim_ids":["clm_1ed1e451ac0798b98b6ec6988e60c30f7fe95b1295ba005cb4d95d63a9a993da","clm_5bb1f3847f4984638c76a18d3c27a8df1cddf1c5ee443a5c338165a44b9d0a38","clm_639ee5fabe7c55abd2aa268bd6483507d749312f36ab51860a108e802933efe4","clm_6920e1412e414365b7e7e3f04f6a409ff062ee2b2d8713a9ea02e329e5c722c7","clm_69f246579dd0af64583445181b87e87579175c693e7815b8d8477d26624cf843","clm_6e0c0c38c0c4e4d787c181c835eee9e04bc4f7681f58cab2beb5430df9300ac9","clm_a300fbc4166ce220b18aafa906be1ee3ecccd6905726b07d1adadc51aaa8f197","clm_ab8341aabfd3ebff291e36f706f043ee5f89a1b5f9cf9286ef4457378de024b1","clm_b24b23ff187da7326df112088f851726de351373db6fce4bdcbec5194197115a","clm_bd5f199b443d927b519e8170830ebb4e569be917b8e713abee7f7923d0a21f1e","clm_d0e8c9ab428966612f3c83877527df401f3cedcfe59eb36b03befe04d55e2c91","clm_de0125b1027710e4759bf0c58e9c6d1703e655f983fcad6e46a975fef87d011b"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T02:01:12Z","created_by_operation":"op_f58d8eef1ae04d8b9b8bb91c9ed483f1","id":"pg_c373b30e1b0f566eb830f1755100a8cc","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/fuxicodex-fuxi-readme-md-ab2785904754-f1755100a8cc.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_887f5d32422a594782426ff7e3450d9f"],"title":"fuxicodex/Fuxi/README.md @ ab2785904754","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:01:12Z","updated_by_operation":"op_f58d8eef1ae04d8b9b8bb91c9ed483f1"}
